WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:16.972
past the market, Vinnie followed Akhom down some stairs.

2
00:00:18.293 --> 00:00:21.654
The chamber below was cool and the air smelled strange.

3
00:00:21.674 --> 00:00:25.556
“Stay right here and wait for me,” Akhom whispered.

4
00:00:26.297 --> 00:00:28.158
Akhom left to look for his father.

5
00:00:29.218 --> 00:00:31.860
“We’re going to see a real mummy, Mandy!”

6
00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:33.252
cried Vinnie.

7
00:00:34.693 --> 00:00:36.473
He turned around to speak to Mandy.

8
00:00:37.253 --> 00:00:39.334
But Mandy was nowhere to be seen.

9
00:00:41.215 --> 00:00:45.116
In a panic, Vinnie left his spot and walked down a dark hallway.

10
00:00:46.176 --> 00:00:48.677
He needed Akhom to help find his sister.

11
00:00:51.378 --> 00:00:54.579
When he heard voices coming from a room, he looked in.

12
00:00:55.859 --> 00:00:59.080
Three men were standing over a body on a flat table.

13
00:01:00.408 --> 00:01:03.150
One of the older men spoke to the youngest person.

14
00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:07.472
Vinnie guessed this must be Akhom’s brother, Tau.

15
00:01:07.932 --> 00:01:12.074
“Tau, please explain what we are going to do.”

16
00:01:13.195 --> 00:01:16.457
Tau replied, “First we will remove the organs.”

17
00:01:17.017 --> 00:01:17.577
He gulped.

18
00:01:17.597 --> 00:01:22.580
“Then we put them in the clay jars.”

19
00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:26.602
He pointed to the jars standing against the wall.

20
00:01:26.622 --> 00:01:29.724
“Then what do we do with the natron?”

21
00:01:30.332 --> 00:01:32.473
The man pointed to a large jar.

22
00:01:33.574 --> 00:01:36.415
It was filled with white powder that looked like salt.

23
00:01:36.435 --> 00:01:40.698
“Put it inside and outside the body,” replied Tau.

24
00:01:40.718 --> 00:01:42.999
“Why?” the man asked.

25
00:01:43.919 --> 00:01:47.821
“So the body won’t spoil while it dries up,” explained Tau.

26
00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:51.123
“When can we wrap it in linen bandages?”

27
00:01:51.844 --> 00:01:52.524
asked the man.

28
00:01:53.825 --> 00:01:55.766
Tau swallowed before answering.

29
00:01:55.786 --> 00:01:57.927
“In forty days, Father.”

30
00:01:57.947 --> 00:02:01.929
“Whoa,” Vinnie said under his breath.

31
00:02:01.949 --> 00:02:04.832
“So that’s how to make a mummy!”

32
00:02:07.374 --> 00:02:09.936
Suddenly, a cold hand touched his arm.

33
00:02:10.657 --> 00:02:12.518
“What are you doing here?”

34
00:02:13.359 --> 00:02:14.720
Akhom whispered angrily.

35
00:02:15.881 --> 00:02:17.842
He pulled Vinnie away from the room.

36
00:02:19.043 --> 00:02:22.867
When they were in the hallway, Vinnie told him about losing Mandy.

37
00:02:22.887 --> 00:02:26.570
“We have to find her,” he said urgently.

38
00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:29.212
“Let’s go, then,” Akhom said.

39
00:02:30.144 --> 00:02:32.867
“When you grow up, do you have to learn that too?”

40
00:02:33.687 --> 00:02:35.569
Vinnie asked, pointing behind him.

41
00:02:35.589 --> 00:02:39.152
“Yes, I must,” replied Akhom.

42
00:02:39.172 --> 00:02:41.374
“My father is an embalmer.

43
00:02:42.235 --> 00:02:44.597
So my brothers and I will be embalmers too.”

44
00:02:45.878 --> 00:02:48.320
Vinnie was glad his dad was an architect.

45
00:02:49.441 --> 00:02:54.105
Meanwhile at the village market, Mandy was wishing she had followed Vinnie.

46
00:02:55.126 --> 00:02:56.988
The fruit seller tried to grab her.

47
00:02:58.076 --> 00:03:00.958
Near her, several men walked in a long line.

48
00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:06.303
Each carried a large bundle of long green sticks on their backs.

49
00:03:07.484 --> 00:03:11.207
Mandy ran into their line, hidden by the men and their bundles.

50
00:03:11.227 --> 00:03:13.428
“Stop! Thief!”

51
00:03:13.969 --> 00:03:14.990
yelled the old man.

52
00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:17.151
“I’m very sorry!”

53
00:03:17.732 --> 00:03:18.773
Mandy called back.

54
00:03:19.773 --> 00:03:23.777
But she walked with the men and their reeds, hidden from her pursuer.

55
00:03:26.279 --> 00:03:27.840
The man in front of her laughed.

56
00:03:28.576 --> 00:03:29.376
“What did you steal?”

57
00:03:30.477 --> 00:03:32.337
“Nothing,” she replied.

58
00:03:33.117 --> 00:03:34.358
She changed the subject.

59
00:03:35.338 --> 00:03:36.598
“What are you carrying?”

60
00:03:36.618 --> 00:03:40.259
“Papyrus reeds, of course,” he answered.

61
00:03:40.279 --> 00:03:42.420
“We’re going to the workshop now.”

62
00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:45.621
“What do you make with papyrus?”

63
00:03:46.361 --> 00:03:47.141
Mandy asked.

64
00:03:48.042 --> 00:03:49.722
The man looked at her strangely.

65
00:03:49.742 --> 00:03:53.183
“Papyrus is used to make paper and other things.

66
00:03:54.483 --> 00:03:56.404
Surely you know that,” he said.

67
00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:02.371
She quickly responded, “I mean, what are you going to make with that papyrus?”

68
00:04:02.391 --> 00:04:05.858
“Come join us and see,” said the friendly man.
